+each full window down a pipe to a separate low-priority process, which runs the
+models and answers with its decision. It is a process and not a thread so that
+a model cannot hold the GIL against the stream: at a 50 ms lead, a chunk has
+little margin to lose. If the worker is busy or dead a window is dropped and the
+preset in use stays, and nothing in the audio path ever waits on it.
+
+The decision comes from EfficientAT mn10 over the whole 5 s window. On 14
+labelled videos (2026-10-31), with the rule below, it was the only one tested
+with no false music on films, games or sport: YAMNet on one patch gave 10 of 96
+film windows, and 100 of 100 on music against mn10's 98. Its margin on real music
+through the TV is thin (0.51 and 0.57 on two clips), so YAMNet's score is logged
+beside it as a reference and has no say.
+
+ONE THREAD IS LOAD-BEARING. Without OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 the mel's matrix
+product spread over every core: 478 ms of CPU a window against 33 (0.76% of a
+thread), and a flat-out run of that coincided with the stream's lead dropping.
+
+Clips are the raw input, before TV mode, as mono 32 kHz WAV, what mn10 hears:
+one when the decision changes, one when a window's label changes (at most one a
